@* The map (03 section 3.4): the element MapLibre draws into, and the empty container of the edge bubbles (EdgeBubbles). Pins, bubbles, chips and zones are
   made by realmMap.js from the payloads this component sends (MapView.razor.cs), never by Razor. The canvas is fixed to the viewport behind the sheet and the navigation
   (01 section 3.3); the inline style is the one place that rule lives until the layout slice moves it into app.css. When the browser has no
   WebGL 2 the canvas is replaced by a plain message and the rest of the page keeps working (03 section 4.4). *@
@if (_webGlUnavailable)
{
    <div class="realm-map-unavailable"
         data-testid="map-unavailable"
         role="status"
         style="position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 16px; text-align: center; color: var(--realm-text-2);">
        @WebGlMessage
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div id="@ContainerId"
         class="realm-map-canvas"
         data-testid="map-canvas"
         role="application"
         aria-label="@MapStrings.Default.MapLabel"
         style="position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 0;"></div>
    <EdgeBubbles />
}
